      <title>National Grid to site biggest substation on Teesside, near planned AI datacentre</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/01/national-grid-to-site-biggest-substation-on-teesside-near-planned-ai-datacentre</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;New electricity generating capacity would enable north-east to attract investment for major datacentre projects&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;National Grid has taken a step towards building Britain’s biggest electricity substation on Teesside, which could supply power to a vast neighbouring datacentre, as the UK races to expand its AI infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Last week the company agreed to purchase 73 acres of land at Dorman Point on a site owned by Teesworks, a local private-public partnership. The deal was first reported by Sky News.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/01/national-grid-to-site-biggest-substation-on-teesside-near-planned-ai-datacentre"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
