      <title>Is AI your new wingman? How chatbots are transforming dating</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2026/oct/31/ai-your-wingman-chatbots-transforming-dating</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Almost 40% of British singles have used AI for romantic advice, from writing messages to assessing potential partners&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;After Sam’s ex joked that her sister found him ugly, he turned to AI. Google Gemini had a look at the photo and politely disagreed. AI has been his wingman ever since, aiding his dating life by giving pep talks and vetting his messages.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The 27-year-old from Stoke-on-Trent is not the only AI-assisted romantic – a survey of 3,000 British singles published this month by Match Group, the owner of the Tinder and Hinge platforms, found 39% had used AI in their dating lives.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2026/oct/31/ai-your-wingman-chatbots-transforming-dating"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
